 "send_at": "2026-09-30T06:00:00-04:00",
 "subject": "Wednesday, Sep 30 - Morning edition",
 "body": "<style>@import url(\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IM+Fell+English&family=Pinyon+Script&family=Source+Serif+4:opsz,wght@8..60,400;8..60,600&display=swap\");a[x-apple-data-detectors]{color:inherit!important;text-decoration:none!important;font-size:inherit!important;font-family:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){.hd-ink{color:#f0ebe2!important}.hd-body{color:#d9d2c5!important}.hd-muted{color:#a59b8a!important}.hd-accent{color:#eb9d82!important}.hd-rule{border-color:#3d3831!important}.hd-inkrule{border-color:#f0ebe2!important}.hd-box{background:#262320!important;background-color:#262320!important;border-color:#3d3831!important}}</style>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td class=\"hd-body\" style=\"padding:6px 4px 20px;color:#3a342c;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5\">\n<p class=\"hd-inkrule hd-ink\" style=\"margin:0;padding:6px 0 5px;border-top:3px double #1d1a16;border-bottom:1px solid #1d1a16;text-align:center;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:9px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#1d1a16\">Spin-free news · Ranked by impact</p>\n<p style=\"margin:16px 0 0;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;line-height:1.1\"><a href=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/\" style=\"text-decoration:none\"><span class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"font-family:'IM Fell English',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:25px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#1d1a16\">HIGH</span> <span class=\"hd-accent\" style=\"font-family:'Pinyon Script','Snell Roundhand',cursive;font-size:31px;margin:0 3px;color:#8b2a1d\">impact</span> <span class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"font-family:'IM Fell English',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:25px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#1d1a16\">NEWS</span> <span class=\"hd-accent\" style=\"font-family:'Pinyon Script','Snell Roundhand',cursive;font-size:31px;margin:0 3px;color:#8b2a1d\">daily</span></a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-head.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"260\" height=\"20\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:260px;max-width:80%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<p class=\"hd-accent\" style=\"margin:18px 0 0;text-align:center;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8b2a1d\">Morning edition · Wednesday, September 30</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:4px 0 6px;text-align:center;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-style:italic;font-size:14px;color:#6b6358\">What happened overnight, and yesterday&#x27;s biggest stories. Five minutes. No spin.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted hd-rule\" style=\"margin:26px 0 0;padding:0 0 6px;border-bottom:1px solid #e2d9c8;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6358\">Overnight</p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:20px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#1d1a16\">Iran received a formal U.S. response to its proposal to end the war and reopen the Strait of Hormuz.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3a342c\">Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi presented the U.S. response to President Masoud Pezeshkian at Wednesday&#x27;s cabinet meeting after receiving feedback via Qatari mediators in Doha on Tuesday night, officials said. The contents were not disclosed. A Reuters-briefed official said the main disagreement is the sequencing of a seven-day trust-building plan, not its components. President Trump had publicly rejected Iran&#x27;s earlier offer days ago; mediators kept working. Pezeshkian said Iran would seek a &quot;win-win&quot; agreement.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6358\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-4.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#1d1a16\">Impact 4/5.</b> Moves ceasefire and Hormuz reopening talks after Trump&#x27;s public rejection; the strait carries about a fifth of the world&#x27;s oil. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.therepublic.com/2026/09/30/iran-indicates-its-received-an-official-us-response-to-its-latest-offer-on-ending-the-war/\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">AP ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#1d1a16\">Russian strikes on Kyiv and the surrounding region overnight killed four people, including a child, and hit power infrastructure.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3a342c\">President Zelenskyy said the main targets were energy infrastructure in Kyiv and the surrounding region. The Russian Defense Ministry claimed hits on a hydroelectric plant, a thermal plant, a substation, an energy storage facility and a data center; Ukrainian officials did not confirm those specific targets and reported hits on civilian areas in at least four Kyiv districts. Ukraine&#x27;s air force said Russia is using ballistic missiles and jet-powered drones that are hard to intercept.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6358\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#1d1a16\">Impact 3/5.</b> Continues Russia&#x27;s campaign against Ukraine&#x27;s power grid ahead of winter; not a change in the war&#x27;s scope. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://thehill.com/homenews/ap/ap-international/ap-russia-pounds-the-kyiv-region-killing-4-and-targeting-the-power-grid/\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">AP ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#1d1a16\">OFAC published a final rule putting 2020 Iran sector sanctions into the Iranian Transactions and Sanctions Regulations, effective Sept. 30.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3a342c\">The rule amends 31 CFR part 560 to implement Executive Order 13902, which authorizes blocking of persons operating in Iran&#x27;s construction, mining, manufacturing or textiles sectors, among other authorities, and adds humanitarian and U.N. official-business exemptions. OFAC has already used E.O. 13902 for designations; this updates the Code of Federal Regulations. Willful violations may carry criminal penalties under IEEPA.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6358\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#1d1a16\">Impact 3/5.</b> A binding final rule, though it largely codifies authorities already used under a 2020 executive order. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/30/2026-19978/iranian-transactions-and-sanctions-regulations\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Federal Register ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#1d1a16\">The Yankees, Braves, Padres and White Sox each won Game 1 of their MLB Wild Card Series on Tuesday.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3a342c\">Yankees beat the Red Sox 9-0; Braves beat the Phillies 5-3; Padres beat the Cubs 8-0; White Sox beat the Astros 6-3. All four series are best-of-three; Game 2s are Wednesday. Teams that take a 1-0 lead have historically won the Wild Card Series about 88% of the time.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6358\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#1d1a16\">Impact 3/5.</b> Sets the early postseason bracket; series continue Wednesday. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.mlb.com/news/yankees-win-al-wild-card-game-1-2026\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">MLB.com / ESPN ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#1d1a16\">The Senate rejected, 47-51, a motion to force a floor vote on a resolution seeking a State Department report on Israel&#x27;s human rights record.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3a342c\">The motion would have discharged S.Res. 852, sponsored by Sen. Chris Van Hollen, from the Foreign Relations Committee under Section 502B of the Foreign Assistance Act. Sen. Rand Paul was the only Republican voting yes; Sen. John Fetterman was the only Democrat voting no. Sens. Cassidy and Sullivan did not vote. The Senate adjourned at 8:15 p.m.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6358\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-2.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#1d1a16\">Impact 2/5.</b> A procedural vote that leaves the resolution in committee; it does not change U.S. policy or aid. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1192/vote_119_2_00252.htm\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">U.S. Senate ↗</a></p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted hd-rule\" style=\"margin:34px 0 0;padding:14px 0 6px;border-top:3px double #e2d9c8;border-bottom:1px solid #e2d9c8;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6358\">Yesterday&#x27;s biggest stories</p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:20px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#1d1a16\">The Transportation Department finalized lower fuel economy standards for new cars and light trucks.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3a342c\">New vehicles must average 34.9 miles per gallon by model year 2031, down from about 50 mpg under the previous rules. The rule covers model years 2022 through 2031, ends the credit-trading program automakers use to meet the standards starting in 2028, and changes how vehicles are classified as cars or light trucks in 2030. The department estimates it lowers the average new-vehicle price by about $1,300. Environmental groups criticized the change.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6358\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-4.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#1d1a16\">Impact 4/5.</b> A final, binding national rule for every new car and light truck sold in the U.S.; it can be challenged in court or changed by a later rule. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.repairerdrivennews.com/2026/09/29/usdot-releases-final-corporate-average-fuel-economy-standards-rule-for-model-years-2022-2031/\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Repairer Driven News ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#1d1a16\">A 100% Section 232 tariff on most patented drug imports took effect for companies not covered by the July phase-in.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3a342c\">Under Proclamation 11020, the additional duties applied to Annex III companies from July 31 and to all other companies&#x27; patented pharmaceuticals and ingredients entered on or after 12:01 a.m. Eastern on Sept. 29. Rates range from 0% to 100% depending on patent status, country, onshoring agreements and use; generics and many U.S.-origin products are excluded. Partner jurisdictions such as the U.K. can face 0%, and EU/Japan/South Korea/Switzerland/Liechtenstein patented articles face 15%.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6358\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-4.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#1d1a16\">Impact 4/5.</b> A binding nationwide tariff on patented drug imports for most remaining companies; it can raise list prices or shift supply chains. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/04/09/2026-06956/adjusting-imports-of-pharmaceuticals-and-pharmaceutical-ingredients-into-the-united-states\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">CBP / Federal Register ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#1d1a16\">The Supreme Court let the administration resume deporting immigrants to countries other than their own while the case continues.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3a342c\">Justices Sotomayor, Kagan and Jackson would have denied the request. The order pauses a Massachusetts federal judge&#x27;s ruling, upheld by the 1st Circuit, that the policy denied immigrants a chance to raise fears of torture or persecution in the destination country. Deportations have included flights to El Salvador, Libya and South Sudan. The court will hear arguments in December, with a decision expected by summer 2027.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6358\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#1d1a16\">Impact 3/5.</b> Deportations can resume now, but the order is temporary: the court hears the case in December and rules by summer 2027. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/supreme-court-trump-third-country-deportation-policy/\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">CBS News ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#1d1a16\">The Energy Department offered to exchange up to 40 million barrels from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3a342c\">The request for proposal is the final tranche of the United States&#x27; 172-million-barrel contribution to a coordinated International Energy Agency release of about 400 million barrels after Middle East supply disruption. Crude would come from the Big Hill and Bryan Mound sites, with deliveries scheduled for November and December 2026; companies must return the oil plus premium barrels. Bids are due Oct. 6. Energy Secretary Chris Wright urged European countries to fulfill their release pledges.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6358\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#1d1a16\">Impact 3/5.</b> Puts more crude into the market while oil and diesel prices remain elevated; it continues a previously announced commitment. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.energy.gov/articles/united-states-energy-department-continues-execution-strategic-reserve-release-commitments\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">U.S. Department of Energy ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#1d1a16\">Treasury sanctioned 10 people and companies it says procured weapons for Iran&#x27;s Defense Ministry.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3a342c\">Under Operation Economic Outcast, OFAC designated individuals and entities in Iran, Hong Kong, China, Pakistan, Saudi Arabia and Turkey tied to procurement for Iran&#x27;s Ministry of Defense and Armed Forces Logistics, including networks supplying electronics for drones and ballistic missiles. The action was taken under E.O. 13382. U.S.-linked assets of the designated persons are blocked.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6358\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;height:16px;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#1d1a16\">Impact 3/5.</b> Expands U.S. economic pressure on Iran&#x27;s wartime military supply chain, but is a targeted designation, not a new nationwide rule. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0637\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">U.S. Treasury ↗</a></p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted hd-rule\" style=\"margin:34px 0 0;padding:14px 0 6px;border-top:3px double #e2d9c8;border-bottom:1px solid #e2d9c8;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6358\">This week so far</p>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td class=\"hd-body hd-rule\" style=\"padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e2d9c8;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;color:#3a342c\">President Trump rejected Iran&#x27;s latest proposal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and end the war. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.justsecurity.org/159075/early-edition-september-28-2026/\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"hd-body hd-rule\" style=\"padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e2d9c8;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;color:#3a342c\">The Education Department restored the 2020 Title IX rules, rescinding the Biden administration&#x27;s 2024 version. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.upi.com/Top_News/US/2026/09/28/trump-administration-education-mcmahon-title-ix-final-rule/9961790618071/\" style=\"color:#8b2a1d;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"hd-body hd-rule\" 